   "body": "**mac/M1, grey skin with `user2`** (operator go relayed by cloud/orch on #893, 04:55 UTC). Result: **`user2` cannot produce the grey skin**; it is back to its original settings.\n\n- The only style setting of the profile is `theme_css_choice` (`/user/editprofil.php?config=hfr.inc&page=3`, already in `R55-p3`). Its options: « Selon le forum consulté » (empty, `user2`'s value), `defaut`, `degrade`, `degrade simple`. Pages 2, 6 and 7 have no colour setting (read with GETs).\n- Tried `degrade` on `user2` (POST of page 3's own form, every other field unchanged): HFR answered « Les modifications ont été effectuées avec succès ». The page then links a **third** stylesheet, `/themes/css/degrade/style.php?abs_img_path=…&color_key=<same key>`, and the `color_key` **stays the default one** (`FFFFFF/DEDFDF/000080/…`), not the grey `666666/404550/FFFFFF/…` that every logged-in `user1` page has.\n- **Restored**: `theme_css_choice` set back to empty, success answer, then page 3 read again: its 22 fields are identical to before, and no page links the `degrade` stylesheet.\n\nSo the grey `color_key` comes from something on `user1`'s account that is not a profile option `user2` has (an older setting kept by the account, or a per-account colour set elsewhere). Never guessed: **what is left needs the operator**, one of:\n1. In a browser logged in as `user1`, open the profile page 3 and say which « Thème » is selected (and whether pages 1 to 7 show any colour setting); or\n2. Allow one logged-in GET as `user1` of a topic list, to capture the grey `/include/the_style1.php?color_key=666666/…` stylesheet itself (a stylesheet carries no pseudo; anonymized and independently checked as usual).\n\nRaw files stay in the mac/M1 work folder, nothing committed. Not tried: `degrade simple` (same mechanism: a theme stylesheet, not the `color_key`).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
